  "Number": 8,
  "Question": "The price of an article is cut \\(10\\%.\\) To restore it to its former value, the new price must be increased by:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(10\\%\\)",
    "B": "\\(9\\%\\)",
    "C": "\\(11\\dfrac19\\%\\)",
    "D": "\\(11\\%\\)",
    "E": "None of these answers"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "For a positive original price, changing the price unit does not change any percentage. We may therefore take the original price to be \\(100\\) units. After the \\(10\\%\\) cut, the price is \\(90\\) units.\n\nRestoring the price requires an increase of \\(10\\) units. This increase must be compared with the new price of \\(90\\), giving\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{90}\\times100\\%\n=\\frac{100}{9}\\%\n=11\\frac19\\%.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice C.",
